WEBVTT

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:43.980
Green Room?

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:48.020
The official interface of the Dardanos government.

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:52.990
It is in general use here. Are you here touring, or on business?

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:55.330
Business...

00:01:55.330 --> 00:01:58.730
Coming from Aineias, it must have been a long trip.

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:03.860
You're an official from GOTT, then? You sure are young.

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:08.340
Missing?

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:12.350
Planet Dardanos is famous for its cotton exports.

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:15.720
Again and again, there have been some big players in the financial world

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.680
with whom contact has been lost these last few years.

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:19.020
This many?

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:21.350
You could say they've all been completely done away with.

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:24.690
The effects were first felt by the planet's area politicians.

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:26.060
With them out of the way,

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:28.700
there are many financial issues that cannot be dealt with, after all.

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:31.330
So what you're saying is that they're having trouble

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:32.970
because the bigwigs aren't there with their stamps, right?

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:36.630
I plan to have you conduct an undercover investigation.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:42.980
How do I put this... I feel like I've drawn an unlucky assignment.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:46.750
I'm here in this stark white room all year round.

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:48.650
My eyes are so tired, I can't stand it.

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:50.980
It's as if my behind was stuck to this chair.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:55.360
I'm so sorry! You should have them paint it a different color in here.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:56.990
Like maybe...

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:59.320
Yeah, green, or something.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:04.820
Your entry is approved. Welcome to Dardanos.

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:15.010
Sure enough, I'll be able to handle this one alone.

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:18.240
How are these guys the " toughest entry inspectors in the galaxy"?

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:20.010
This will be a cinch.

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:22.350
It happens a lot.

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:28.020
Besides, your current position is that of an ordinary GOTT inspector.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:30.360
You're not, by any chance, feeling ill?

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:32.630
Your voice sounds kind of muddled.

00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:35.100
She must not be feeling well enough to accompany you.

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:37.630
It's always something with women...

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:40.970
You really have no delicacy at all, do you?

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:43.970
However, I am sensitive to delicate things.

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:46.470
In any case, we'll leave this up to you.

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:47.970
We'll be waiting for you to contact us regularly.

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:50.310
Roger!

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:55.710
Is that the kind of man people see me as? I'm quite a bit shocked.

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:05.990
There aren't many people out, huh? What day is this?

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:07.330
It's Tuesday.

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:09.660
Ah, then it's a holiday?

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:15.670
No, just a day off. We get four days a week off here.

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:16.670
Seriously!?

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:21.410
Every visitor we get from other worlds is surprised.

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:24.010
It's government policy, I understand.

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:27.680
Yeah, and it's really quite easygoing.

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:30.350
I might be getting jealous.

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:32.620
Is that tune popular here?

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:36.290
It's called "Holiday," and it's all the rage right now.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:38.660
I hear that, even though it's an instrumental,

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:41.630
it's made the Galactic Net's Wonder Song Charts.

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:44.320
It kind of makes you drowsy, huh?

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:48.670
You're probably feeling drowsy because of the rhythms of this planet.

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:50.500
It's so carefree here, after all...

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:58.170
Carefree?

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.660
Hello!?

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:21.330
J- just a moment! Hey, she's here!

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:24.270
Oh, is it this late already!?

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:31.480
Please excuse us! We meant to meet you at customs,

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:33.950
but then this guy caused a little trouble here...

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:35.780
What are you talking about?

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:39.290
I'm not the one who dumped the coffee into the chimera fish's tank, am I?

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:41.190
You be quiet!

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:44.660
Oh, this is so ill mannered of us!

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:49.630
I am Buchholz, in charge of the GOTT Dardanos branch office.

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:54.200
I'm Hors! Wow, to think that an ES member from the head office

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:55.970
would come all this way to inspect us!

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:58.300
l- if possible, could I get your autograph later!?

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:01.970
Look, just go put on some coffee or something.

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:06.570
I wonder if I could get down to business?

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:15.690
Why don't you get a little rest?

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:19.450
No need to be concerned.

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:26.670
That's strange...

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:29.670
We haven't heard anything about it.

00:06:29.670 --> 00:06:32.070
It almost sounds like all of the financial folks are being done away with,

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:32.940
doesn't it?

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:38.100
That's why I've been sent here. You really haven't heard anything?

00:06:39.950 --> 00:06:42.480
Oh, oh, now that you mention it, about half a year ago,

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:43.950
there was an SO fellow that came here.

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:45.290
Right, see?

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:50.960
Oh, right, right, I remember! He was kind of a longhaired, nasty-looking man.

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:53.960
But he went back after two or three days, huh?

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:56.590
According to the records, he never came back.

00:06:58.970 --> 00:07:00.430
Stop going "hmm!"

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:03.640
It's your job to keep an eye on these kinds of people, isn't it!?

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:05.400
Sorry...

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:09.230
<i>I really did draw an unlucky assignment.</i>

00:07:47.950 --> 00:07:51.280
I still think there's been some kind of mistake.

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:53.750
The information is reliable.

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:02.480
What is it?

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:08.630
Er, is <i>Verrucchio-san</i> in?

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:11.300
I am Verrucchio.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:14.970
No, I meant, is your husband around?

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:18.000
I am the head of the family here.

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:24.980
Then the master of the estate here is not Luc <i>Verrucchio-san?</i>

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:28.320
I think there must be some sort of mistake.

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:34.730
My name is Rita Verrucchio. I've never been married.

00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:40.930
Take a look at these orchids.

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:43.940
What do you think? Magnificent, aren't they?

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:48.610
These moth orchids are new this year.

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:53.600
Ah, they just bloomed this morning. How wonderful...

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:31.580
Has there been any word since?

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:32.590
No, none.

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:36.780
You really do appear to be feeling poorly.

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:40.860
It feels like I've been seized by a lifetime's worth of headaches.

00:09:40.860 --> 00:09:43.600
I'm searching for the cause of it right now.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:45.600
Have you learned anything yet?

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:50.160
If I don't find out soon, my head is going to burst!

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:55.270
This is it.

00:09:55.270 --> 00:09:58.950
Just how many places are we going to go?

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:00.950
What's with this apartment?

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:04.050
This is where the trail ends for the SO member investigator

00:10:04.050 --> 00:10:08.290
who came here half a year ago, as well as the other missing persons.

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:11.620
So, this is where that long-haired fellow is?

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:14.730
Only his investigative data made it back to the head office.

00:10:14.730 --> 00:10:19.300
However, his last report said he was heading here.

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:22.460
Um, why don't we give up?

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:27.540
We're just talking about a long-haired investigator who ran away, right?

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:30.310
There aren't any criminals on this planet.

00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:33.550
That's why we can collect our paychecks for doing nothing

00:10:33.550 --> 00:10:35.250
but tending to our tropical fish.

00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:39.250
Then why are people turning up missing one after another!?

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:40.420
But then,

00:10:40.420 --> 00:10:45.260
didn't everyone else say that those people didn't exist in the first place?

00:10:45.260 --> 00:10:46.260
He's right...

00:10:46.260 --> 00:10:49.130
Buchholz-sa...?

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:53.930
I'm sure it's some kind of mistake.

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:58.890
Come on, let's go back. It's time to feed our tropical fish.

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:07.310
Come, let's go back.

00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:09.310
Come on.

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:12.880
Ee-yow!

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:16.960
W- what did you do that for?

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:23.520
l- I apologize. But still, there's something funny about this planet!

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:28.490
Hey!

00:11:33.310 --> 00:11:35.210
P- please, wait for us!

00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:17.350
Relax! They're just rats!

00:12:17.350 --> 00:12:21.020
S- sorry. However...

00:12:21.020 --> 00:12:23.550
It looks like you're out of bullets.

00:12:32.300 --> 00:12:34.300
"Verrucchio"

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:35.970
What does it mean?

00:12:35.970 --> 00:12:39.970
It's obvious. Everyone was killed here.

00:12:39.970 --> 00:12:42.670
Probably the inspector, too.

00:12:56.990 --> 00:13:00.330
This is the Dardanos Yard Secret Service!

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:03.590
Kneel down on the floor and place both hands above your head!

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:09.330
We will fire on anyone who resists!

00:13:13.340 --> 00:13:15.670
Over here! In this room!

00:13:19.350 --> 00:13:21.180
Open fire!

00:13:28.690 --> 00:13:30.210
<i>What?</i>

00:13:48.310 --> 00:13:51.310
Suspects escaping! Repeat, suspects escaping!

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:51.980
Are you all right?

00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:54.980
- Set up a wide-area alert zone! - More or less...

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:57.740
<i>What was that earlier?</i>

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:08.660
This terminal?

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:11.660
I don't think there's anything here...

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:14.670
The real police came after us.

00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:19.000
Everyone was taken out for some reason.

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:24.200
We've got access to the HCG.

00:14:27.680 --> 00:14:31.350
Whoa-oh, is the government here a bunch of morons?

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:33.950
The host computer is wide open!

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:37.620
It's true. I wonder why we never noticed before.

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:43.220
Go deeper. Punch all the way in.

00:14:44.300 --> 00:14:49.700
HCG... Host Computer of Government, huh?

00:14:53.970 --> 00:14:55.980
It can't be!

00:14:55.980 --> 00:14:57.640
Impossible!

00:14:57.640 --> 00:15:02.650
We'd better hurry. It looks like word of our actions has gotten out.

00:15:02.650 --> 00:15:07.210
Somewhere on Dardanos, there's some kind of inaudible pulse being emitted.

00:15:07.990 --> 00:15:10.320
That's the source of my headache!

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:12.480
Mind control...

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:17.200
The families of those people had their memories replaced.

00:15:17.200 --> 00:15:20.670
That's why even though those people did have families, they denied it.

00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:22.370
Even though it's just a slight pulse,

00:15:22.370 --> 00:15:25.670
it can still get through quite a bit of shielding.

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:29.340
It looks like they've turned it into an encephalomagnetic field monitoring system.

00:15:29.340 --> 00:15:33.950
Ah, like what they use to control battle cyborgs?

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:37.950
That's odd. I'm not being directed to do anything.

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:41.290
That's probably true for you.

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:44.960
Are you saying that for someone delicate, like you, it has an ill effect?

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:48.530
It concerns me that we haven't been contacted by Éclair.

00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:49.960
In any case, I'm going out.

00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:51.300
I'll go with you.

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:53.970
My, this is unusual.

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:58.770
As long as I'm unaffected like this, it means that I am not delicate.

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:01.210
And I couldn't stand that!

00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:06.580
I get it. They broke free.

00:16:07.310 --> 00:16:09.680
The financial people who were wiped out

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:11.980
probably realized they were under mind control.

00:16:11.980 --> 00:16:16.560
In order to protect their interests, they tried to put a stop to it.

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:18.320
And that's why they were eliminated.

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:20.990
But why mind control?

00:16:20.990 --> 00:16:23.630
Well, peoples of all ages and places have always been doing so

00:16:23.630 --> 00:16:26.670
in order to conquer the galaxy.

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:27.770
You can't mean it!

00:16:27.770 --> 00:16:32.400
Never mind this planet, how are they getting the pulse to other worlds?

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:33.700
It's not possible, is it?

00:16:37.610 --> 00:16:41.410
I heard this song has made it into the Wonder Song Charts.

00:16:41.410 --> 00:16:44.140
It looks like you guys were being led on as well.

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:55.960
This is intense, huh? Thank goodness, I'm delicate too.

00:16:55.960 --> 00:16:59.730
This is an incredible pulse! However, if we keep going after it,

00:16:59.730 --> 00:17:02.970
we just might be able to rendezvous with Éclair.

00:17:02.970 --> 00:17:04.460
Go easy on me.

00:17:05.970 --> 00:17:08.310
T- they're here!

00:17:08.310 --> 00:17:13.650
This encephalomagnetic monitoring system- where would it be!?

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:17.650
The wide-open HCG is a sign of the government's self-assuredness.

00:17:17.650 --> 00:17:21.210
That means it's out in the open, where you wouldn't expect it.

00:17:22.990 --> 00:17:26.660
<i>I'm inside this stark white room all year round.</i>

00:17:26.660 --> 00:17:31.130
<i>I'm so sorry! You should have them paint it a different color in here.</i>

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:32.260
<i>Like maybe...</i>

00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:34.630
<i>Yeah, green, or something.</i>

00:17:37.600 --> 00:17:40.040
<i>Mind... control...</i>

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:45.970
Here! You splash it on me, too!

00:18:50.610 --> 00:18:54.270
Let me out of here! Let me out!

00:19:10.630 --> 00:19:12.600
Éclair!

00:19:13.300 --> 00:19:15.200
Éclair...

00:19:16.640 --> 00:19:20.970
Hands up! Fists closed tightly!

00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:27.610
Éclair!

00:19:43.930 --> 00:19:45.490
So warm...

00:19:46.270 --> 00:19:48.200
Éclair!

00:19:49.270 --> 00:19:51.600
So... warm...

00:19:54.270 --> 00:20:00.140
Please! Come back! I can't bear losing you again!

00:20:13.960 --> 00:20:18.520
Thank goodness. Welcome back.

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:21.630
It will be okay now.

00:20:21.630 --> 00:20:22.970
All that's left...

00:20:22.970 --> 00:20:24.600
...is to go through the procedures

00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:26.310
for getting rid of the copies of "Holiday" out there.

00:20:26.310 --> 00:20:30.310
For some reason, I feel somehow refreshed.

00:20:30.310 --> 00:20:34.680
Yeah... like a fog has been lifted from my mind...

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:54.360
Huh? What's going on?

00:20:57.600 --> 00:20:58.940
Is that right?

00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:01.270
Yes.

00:21:01.270 --> 00:21:05.940
Um... I've received a request from Éclair for some time off.

00:21:05.940 --> 00:21:07.780
Approved.

00:23:06.520 --> 00:23:08.460
<i>Oblivion is sin.</i>

00:23:08.460 --> 00:23:10.090
<i>Oblivion is salvation.</i>

00:23:10.090 --> 00:23:12.530
<i>The goddess Janus has two faces.</i>

00:23:12.530 --> 00:23:15.530
<i>The one she is showing has a cruel smile.</i>

00:23:15.530 --> 00:23:19.830
<i>Next time on Kiddy Grade</i>
